      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by expressing the integer \\( N \\) in terms of its division by 15. Since the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 15 is 7, we can write:\n\\[ N = 15k + 7 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the remainders when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. We do this by substituting \\( N = 15k + 7 \\) into these division problems.\n\n1. **Finding the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3:**\n   \\[ N = 15k + 7 \\]\n   Since \\( 15k \\) is a multiple of 3, it contributes nothing to the remainder when divided by 3. Therefore, we only need to consider the remainder when 7 is divided by 3:\n   \\[ 7 \\div 3 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n   So, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\n2. **Finding the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5:**\n   Again, we only need to consider the remainder when 7 is divided by 5:\n   \\[ 7 \\div 5 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n   So, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of these remainders:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the remainders when the same integer is divided by 3 and by 5 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
