      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "When an integer \\( n \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\]\n\nWe need to find the remainders when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. Let's start with the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3.\n\nSince \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) for some integer \\( k \\), we can substitute this into the expression for the remainder when divided by 3:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 3. Performing the division, we get:\n\\[ 7 = 3 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\nNext, let's find the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5. Again, we substitute \\( n = 15k + 7 \\) into the expression for the remainder when divided by 5:\n\\[ n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 7 is divided by 5. Performing the division, we get:\n\\[ 7 = 5 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThus, the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\nThe sum of the remainders when the integer \\( n \\) is divided by 3 and by 5 is:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
